---
import Article from '../layouts/Article.astro';
import { site, publisher, disclosure } from '../site.config';
---
<Article
  title="Corrections and removal"
  description="How to request a correction to a guide page or a company listing on Bolivia Unpacked, or the removal of a company page."
  path="/corrections/"
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Corrections and removal', path: '/corrections/' }]}
  published={site.launchDate}
  reviewed={site.launchDate}
  sources={[]}
  rail={false}
  kicker="Corrections"
>
  <h2>Company listings</h2>
  <p>Company facts come from the Tourground directory, so they are corrected there, and the change reaches this site at the next build. If you are a company, or anyone who has spotted an error on a company page, use the main site's form:</p>
  <p><a href={publisher.correctionUrl}><strong>{disclosure.correctionLinkText}</strong></a></p>
  <p>Companies can also ask for their page to be removed through the same form. When a company is removed from the directory, its page here is unpublished in the next build.</p>
  <h2>Guide and question pages</h2>
  <p>If a guide or question page is wrong or out of date, email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> with the page address, what is wrong and, if you can, a source. We check the source, correct the page and update its "last reviewed" date.</p>
  <h2>Corrections log</h2>
  <p>No corrections have been made since the site launched on {site.launchDate}.</p>
</Article>
